---
import "../../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <title>Public Slice — 2026-08-07</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A bounded artistic-research reading of four repository-grounded states in public form, permission, preservation and formal authority." />
  <style>
    :root { --deep:#15130f; --raised:#24211c; --max:920px; }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    html{background:var(--bg);scroll-behavior:smooth}
    body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7}
    a{color:var(--link);text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px}
    a:hover{color:var(--link-hover)}
    a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--link);outline-offset:4px;border-radius:2px}
    h1,h2,h3{margin:0;color:var(--text);font-weight:600;line-height:1.22}
    p{margin:0}
    code{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:var(--accent);background:transparent;padding:0}
    main{max-width:var(--max);margin:0 auto;padding:72px 24px 96px}
    .kicker,.label{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.085em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .kicker{color:var(--link);margin-bottom:14px}
    .label{color:var(--muted)}

    .slice-head{max-width:760px;padding-bottom:42px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .slice-head h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.45rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;max-width:16ch;color:var(--accent)}
    .framing{margin-top:20px;max-width:42rem;font-size:1.04rem}
    .date-row{display:flex;gap:34px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:26px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem}
    .date-row span{display:block;margin-bottom:2px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase}

    .slice-index{margin-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .slice-index ol{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
    .slice-index li+li{border-left:1px solid var(--line)}
    .slice-index a{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;padding:12px 10px;color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font-size:.84rem}
    .slice-index a:hover{background:var(--deep)}
    .slice-index b{color:var(--link);font-size:.76rem;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.05em}

    .sequence{margin-top:42px}
    .state{scroll-margin-top:20px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:132px minmax(0,1fr);gap:30px;padding:54px 0 64px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .state:first-child{border-top:0}
    .state-meta{position:sticky;top:24px;align-self:start}
    .state-num{color:var(--link);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.08em}
    .state-verb{margin-top:7px;color:var(--link);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .state-date{margin-top:8px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.45}
    .state h2{max-width:31ch;font-size:clamp(1.45rem,3vw,2rem);letter-spacing:-.02em}
    .state-summary{margin-top:13px;max-width:45rem}

    figure{margin:30px 0 0}
    figcaption{margin-top:10px;max-width:46rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.5}
    .figure-label{margin-bottom:10px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}

    .anchor-figure{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .anchor-side{padding:20px 18px 22px 0}
    .anchor-side+ .anchor-side{padding-left:24px;border-left:2px solid var(--accent)}
    .anchor-side h3{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--link)}
    .anchor-side ul{margin:9px 0 0;padding-left:1.05rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.91rem}
    .anchor-side li{margin:4px 0}

    .freeze-figure{position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;align-items:center;min-height:124px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .freeze-node{text-align:center;padding:20px 12px}
    .freeze-node strong{display:block;color:var(--text);font-size:1rem}
    .freeze-node span{display:block;margin-top:4px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem}
    .freeze-node:nth-child(2){border-left:1px solid var(--line);border-right:1px solid var(--line)}
    .lock{width:42px;height:42px;margin:0 auto 8px}
    .lock path,.lock rect{stroke:var(--link);fill:none;stroke-width:2}

    .identity{margin-top:14px;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px dashed var(--line);border-bottom:1px dashed var(--line);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:var(--muted);font-size:.79rem;line-height:1.65;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
    .identity b{color:var(--text);font-weight:500}

    .coexist-figure{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 120px 1fr;align-items:stretch;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .co-state{padding:22px 0}
    .co-state:last-child{text-align:right}
    .co-count{color:var(--text);font-size:3rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1}
    .co-state h3{margin-top:8px;font-size:.95rem}
    .co-state p{margin-top:5px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}
    .co-mid{display:grid;place-items:center;border-left:1px solid var(--line);border-right:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--link);text-align:center;font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1.55}
    .prepared-note{margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem}

    .radial-figure{border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:12px 0 8px}
    .radial-figure svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:380px}
    .r-edge{stroke:#50493e;stroke-width:1.15;fill:none;opacity:.95}
    .r-ring{stroke:#4a443a;stroke-width:1.35;fill:none}
    .r-ring-a{stroke:var(--link);stroke-width:2;fill:none}
    .r-node{fill:var(--surface);stroke:#b4aa9a;stroke-width:1.45}
    .r-node-a{fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--link);stroke-width:1.8}
    .r-label{fill:var(--muted);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em}
    .r-label-a{fill:var(--link);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;font-weight:700}
    .authority-line{margin-top:12px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:14px;align-items:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:.76rem}
    .authority-line::before{content:"";height:1px;background:var(--link)}

    .raw{margin-top:17px;display:flex;gap:10px 18px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:var(--muted);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:.75rem}
    .raw strong{color:var(--text);font-weight:500}
    .raw a{font-family:inherit}

    .reading{margin-top:24px}
    .reading-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:142px minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .reading-row:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .reading-row dt{color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .reading-row dd{margin:0;max-width:46rem}
    .reading-row.reading-interpretation dd{color:var(--text)}
    .reading-row.reading-interpretation dt{color:var(--link)}
    .reading-row.reading-limit dd{color:var(--muted);font-size:.91rem}

    details{margin-top:15px}
    summary{cursor:pointer;width:fit-content;color:var(--link);font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600}
    .evidence{margin-top:11px;padding-left:16px;border-left:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:.83rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
    .evidence p+p{margin-top:7px}
    .evidence strong{color:var(--text);font-weight:500}

    .synthesis{margin-top:18px;padding-top:46px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .synthesis h2{margin-top:8px;max-width:31ch;font-size:clamp(1.45rem,3vw,2rem)}
    .question{margin-top:20px;max-width:44rem;font-size:1.04rem}
    .question strong{font-weight:600;color:var(--text)}
    .permissions-scope{margin-top:22px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}
    .permissions{margin-top:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .permission{display:grid;grid-template-columns:105px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:11px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:.88rem}
    .permission strong{color:var(--link);font-weight:650}
    .permission span{color:var(--muted)}
    .formula{margin-top:18px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}
    .formula span{display:block;margin-top:3px;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:var(--muted)}
    .boundary-note{margin-top:20px;max-width:48rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem}
    .return{margin-top:46px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:.9rem}
    footer{max-width:var(--max);margin:0 auto;padding:30px 24px 60px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:.83rem}

    @media(max-width:760px){
      main{padding:50px 18px 74px}.slice-head h1{font-size:2.2rem}.slice-index ol{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.slice-index li:nth-child(3){border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.slice-index li:nth-child(4){border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
      .state{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:13px;padding:44px 0 50px}.state-meta{position:static;display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap}.state-verb,.state-date{margin-top:0}
      .anchor-figure{grid-template-columns:1fr}.anchor-side+ .anchor-side{padding-left:0;border-left:0;border-top:2px solid var(--accent)}
      .freeze-figure{grid-template-columns:1fr}.freeze-node:nth-child(2){border-left:0;border-right:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
      .coexist-figure{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;grid-template-areas:"left right" "mid mid";column-gap:16px}.co-state:first-child{grid-area:left}.co-state:last-child{grid-area:right;text-align:right}.co-mid{grid-area:mid;min-height:34px;border-left:0;border-right:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:0}.co-count{font-size:2.45rem}.co-state h3{font-size:.88rem}.co-state p{font-size:.76rem}
      .reading-row{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}.permission{grid-template-columns:82px 1fr}
    }
    @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <header class="slice-head">
    <p class="kicker">Artistic Research / Public Slice</p>
    <h1>Public Slice — 2026-08-07</h1>
    <p class="framing">Four fixed repository states are assembled here into a bounded reading of public form, permission, preservation and formal authority. The evidence establishes each state at a fixed commit; the synthesis is an authored reading of them.</p>
    <div class="date-row">
      <div><span>Slice date</span>7 August 2026</div>
      <div><span>Evidence states</span>30 June–27 July 2026, UTC+8</div>
      <div><span>Indexing</span>noindex / bounded reading</div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav class="slice-index" aria-label="Four states">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#anchor"><b>01</b> Anchor</a></li>
      <li><a href="#freeze"><b>02</b> Freeze</a></li>
      <li><a href="#accumulate"><b>03</b> Accumulate</a></li>
      <li><a href="#recompose"><b>04</b> Recompose</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section class="sequence" aria-label="Four repository-grounded states">
    <article class="state" id="anchor">
      <aside class="state-meta"><div class="state-num">01</div><div class="state-verb">Anchor</div><div class="state-date">30 June 2026</div></aside>
      <div>
        <h2>At this commit, a Public Anchor has a defined scaffold and schema</h2>
        <p class="state-summary">A Public Anchor scaffold and schema are introduced: a named, citable, source-visible record that declares its own scope and non-scope.</p>

        <figure>
          <div class="figure-label">Boundary as form</div>
          <div class="anchor-figure">
            <div class="anchor-side"><h3>May provide</h3><ul><li>public name and classification status</li><li>minimal formulation and related terms</li><li>citation and source-navigation placement</li></ul></div>
            <div class="anchor-side"><h3>Must not stand for</h3><ul><li>the full model or complete protocol</li><li>the full internal registry or working corpus</li><li>a replacement for source-level reading</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <figcaption>The line is not decoration: this reading treats the declared boundary itself as part of the public object.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="raw"><strong>553b341b0b28</strong><span>PUBLIC_ANCHOR_SCHEMA.md</span><span>SOURCE_BOUNDARY_STATEMENT.md</span><span>CITATION.cff</span></div>

        <dl class="reading">
          <div class="reading-row"><dt>Observed state</dt><dd>At this commit a Public Anchor scaffold and schema are present, and they declare scope and non-scope explicitly. For public anchors, visibility alone is not treated as sufficient.</dd></div>
          <div class="reading-row reading-interpretation"><dt>Research reading</dt><dd>The shift is not that publicness as a whole becomes defined, but that the conditions for one kind of public object are formalized.</dd></div>
          <div class="reading-row reading-limit"><dt>Limit</dt><dd>This commit establishes a scaffold and schema. It does not demonstrate a complete population of mature anchor instances or define the whole public surface.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <details><summary>Repository evidence</summary><div class="evidence"><p><strong>Commit:</strong> <code>553b341b0b2840633b5ea33410bec0527679d58d</code> &mdash; <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/tree/553b341b0b2840633b5ea33410bec0527679d58d/public-anchors">browse <code>public-anchors/</code> at this commit</a></p><p><strong>Files:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/553b341b0b2840633b5ea33410bec0527679d58d/public-anchors/PUBLIC_ANCHOR_SCHEMA.md">PUBLIC_ANCHOR_SCHEMA.md</a>, <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/553b341b0b2840633b5ea33410bec0527679d58d/public-anchors/SOURCE_BOUNDARY_STATEMENT.md">SOURCE_BOUNDARY_STATEMENT.md</a>, <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/553b341b0b2840633b5ea33410bec0527679d58d/CITATION.cff">CITATION.cff</a></p><p>Public visibility does not equal full release; citation availability does not equal source completeness.</p></div></details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="state" id="freeze">
      <aside class="state-meta"><div class="state-num">02</div><div class="state-verb">Freeze</div><div class="state-date">25 July 2026, 21:24 UTC+8</div></aside>
      <div>
        <h2>At this commit, the generated view is documented as a historical artifact</h2>
        <p class="state-summary">The tracked 30-record authority-map artifact is made verify-only. Later tooling may check its pinned identity; regeneration in place is outside the documented operations.</p>

        <figure>
          <div class="figure-label">Archival operation</div>
          <div class="freeze-figure">
            <div class="freeze-node"><strong>generator</strong><span>generation capability</span></div>
            <div class="freeze-node"><svg class="lock" viewBox="0 0 42 42" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 18v-5a8 8 0 0 1 16 0v5"/><rect x="9" y="18" width="24" height="18" rx="4"/></svg><strong>30-record artifact</strong><span>historical / pinned</span></div>
            <div class="freeze-node"><strong>verification</strong><span>read / compare / write nothing</span></div>
          </div>
          <figcaption>Verification is the only documented operation on this historical artifact.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="identity"><b>records</b> 30 &nbsp;&nbsp; <b>bytes</b> 92903<br><b>sha256</b> 3b1e5993a52cbce340b85472fea1ae5ea6f921cf8f7751d2d635edc7b17216ea<br><b>mode</b> verify-only &nbsp;&nbsp; <b>write</b> nothing</div>
        <div class="raw"><strong>77f97de50612</strong><span>30 records</span><span>verify-only</span><span>writes nothing</span></div>

        <dl class="reading">
          <div class="reading-row"><dt>Observed state</dt><dd>At this commit the tracked visualization is declared verify-only: its identity values are pinned, and the documented operations read and compare it but write nothing.</dd></div>
          <div class="reading-row reading-interpretation"><dt>Research reading</dt><dd>Preservation is expressed as a permission boundary: future tooling retains the right to verify this past state, but not the right to rewrite it.</dd></div>
          <div class="reading-row reading-limit"><dt>Limit</dt><dd>This establishes historical isolation for this artifact and these repository operations. It is not, by itself, a general archival policy for all MWE material.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <details><summary>Repository evidence</summary><div class="evidence"><p><strong>Commit:</strong> <code>77f97de50612360de48b78b6364f29ef74499900</code> &mdash; <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/tree/77f97de50612360de48b78b6364f29ef74499900/visualizations/public-surface-authority-map">browse <code>public-surface-authority-map/</code> at this commit</a></p><p><strong>File:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/77f97de50612360de48b78b6364f29ef74499900/visualizations/public-surface-authority-map/README.md">public-surface-authority-map/README.md</a></p></div></details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="state" id="accumulate">
      <aside class="state-meta"><div class="state-num">03</div><div class="state-verb">Accumulate</div><div class="state-date">25 July 2026, 23:04 UTC+8</div></aside>
      <div>
        <h2>A later visualization state is documented beside the frozen one</h2>
        <p class="state-summary">A 59-record adjacency dataset is documented as a separate visualization product. It does not replace, supersede, correct or deprecate the frozen 30-node product.</p>

        <figure>
          <div class="figure-label">Temporal coexistence</div>
          <div class="coexist-figure">
            <div class="co-state"><div class="co-count">30</div><h3>Frozen authority-map artifact</h3><p>historical / pinned / independently verifiable</p></div>
            <div class="co-mid">stands beside<br>not over</div>
            <div class="co-state"><div class="co-count">59</div><h3>Expanded adjacency dataset</h3><p>separate product / later selection / prepared data</p></div>
          </div>
          <p class="prepared-note">At this commit the 59-record product is prepared data only; no page publication has occurred.</p>
          <figcaption>The page leaves both states visible at once because coexistence, rather than replacement, is the material under examination.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="raw"><strong>39c7f8b37ba5</strong><span>30 frozen</span><span>59 separate product</span><span>does not supersede</span></div>
        <dl class="reading">
          <div class="reading-row"><dt>Observed state</dt><dd>At this commit a 59-record visualization product is documented beside the frozen 30-node product rather than as its replacement.</dd></div>
          <div class="reading-row reading-interpretation"><dt>Research reading</dt><dd>Within this visualization lineage, a later public state can be added without retroactively erasing the earlier artifact.</dd></div>
          <div class="reading-row reading-limit"><dt>Limit</dt><dd>Coexistence is established for these two products. The later product is prepared data at this commit, and this does not establish a rule that every future representation must be preserved.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <details><summary>Repository evidence</summary><div class="evidence"><p><strong>Commit:</strong> <code>39c7f8b37ba5a63716fcf71b721a4270982a1d6a</code> &mdash; <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/tree/39c7f8b37ba5a63716fcf71b721a4270982a1d6a/visualizations/public-surface-adjacency-map">browse <code>public-surface-adjacency-map/</code> at this commit</a></p><p><strong>File:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/39c7f8b37ba5a63716fcf71b721a4270982a1d6a/visualizations/public-surface-adjacency-map/README.md">public-surface-adjacency-map/README.md</a></p><p>Registry selection and visualization membership remain separate contracts; visual position and membership do not imply formal classification or authority.</p></div></details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="state" id="recompose">
      <aside class="state-meta"><div class="state-num">04</div><div class="state-verb">Recompose</div><div class="state-date">27 July 2026</div></aside>
      <div>
        <h2>At this commit, the interface's form is not assigned formal authority</h2>
        <p class="state-summary">The expanded public surface is presented as a deterministic radial interface with authored record order, keyboard navigation, grouping arcs and routed edges. Rendering constraints limit what geometry, ordering and colour are permitted to formally encode.</p>

        <figure>
          <div class="figure-label">Page-local schematic / not repository evidence</div>
          <div class="radial-figure">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 760 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="rt rd">
              <title id="rt">Schematic of a radial public-surface encounter</title>
              <desc id="rd">A radial field of nodes and selected edges, followed by an authority ceiling line. The diagram is an authored schematic and not a reproduction of repository pixels.</desc>
              <g>
                <circle class="r-ring-a" cx="380" cy="174" r="42"/><circle class="r-ring" cx="380" cy="174" r="82"/><circle class="r-ring" cx="380" cy="174" r="122"/>
                <path class="r-edge" d="M380 52 Q430 115 496 112"/><path class="r-edge" d="M496 112 Q458 178 500 235"/><path class="r-edge" d="M500 235 Q425 236 414 294"/><path class="r-edge" d="M414 294 Q365 242 303 283"/><path class="r-edge" d="M303 283 Q300 212 256 232"/><path class="r-edge" d="M256 232 Q310 170 259 116"/><path class="r-edge" d="M259 116 Q333 126 380 52"/>
                <path class="r-edge" d="M380 132 L496 112"/><path class="r-edge" d="M380 132 L256 232"/><path class="r-edge" d="M380 216 L500 235"/><path class="r-edge" d="M380 216 L259 116"/>
